*   **style_aggression_rating**: VXR styling includes aggressive bumpers, air intakes, gills, prominent roof spoiler, twin Remus exhaust, large wheels. Described as "ruder, lairier and louder", "demonic look", "aggressive styling", "angry little car". Score: 0.70.
*   **style_modernity_rating**: Corsa E design (2014-2019) with VXR styling. Looks reasonably modern but not cutting-edge compared to the current facelifted model. Score: 0.00.
*   **handling_rating**: Features Koni FSD suspension and sports suspension. Performance Pack adds Drexler LSD and retuned Koni dampers. Described as having "magnificent handling", "sharper handling", "lots of grip", "precise athleticism, outstanding and agile handling", "unbeatable traction" with LSD, "lively thing which feels very rewarding when driven at speed". However, also mentions "squirms about under acceleration", "a bit soft" without Performance Pack, "constant battle" with torque steer. Score: 0.50.
*   **ride_comfort_rating**: Koni FSD suspension aims to balance comfort and handling. Described as "very firm", "punishingly hard and abrupt" with Performance Pack, "bone-jarring chassis" for some. Standard car is "noticeably more comfortable". Score: -0.50.
*   **cabin_noise_rating**: Frustrating amount of road noise on the motorway. Engine can sound hard-worked at high revs, but doesn't drone. Score: -0.20.
*   **shift_smooth_rating**: 6-speed manual, described as a "heavily revised, short-shifting lever which is an absolute joy to use", "delight". Score: 0.50.
*   **steering_feel_rating**: Speed-Sensitive Electric Power-Assisted Steering with UK-specific tune. Described as having an "unpleasant stiction just off centre", lacking precise feedback, "firework steering thrills" with LSD, "nicely set-up system too, feeling direct and accurate but also well weighted for enthusiastic driving". Score: 0.00.
*   **adas_score**: Includes ABS, ESP, Six airbags, Hill start assist, Cruise Control, Speed Limiter, Tyre pressure monitoring system. Optional Technical Pack added Forward Collision Alert, Traffic Sign Recognition, Lane Departure Warning, Anti-dazzle rear view mirror, Rear view camera, Following Distance Indicator. Score based on standard features. Score: -0.20.
*   **visibility_rating**: 3-door body style can hinder visibility. Score: -0.10.
*   **headlight_rating**: LED daytime running lights standard. Bi-xenon headlights standard. Score: 0.50.
*   **security_rating**: Remote control security alarm system standard. Basic security for its time, but older Corsas are known targets. Scored poorly in anti-theft tests by Thatcham Research (Poor rating for relay attack). Score: -0.50.
*   **screen_in**: R4.0 IntelliLink infotainment system standard. This is a 7-inch touchscreen. Score: -0.20.
*   **infotainment_ux_rating**: IntelliLink system was decent for its time, but not as slick as modern systems. Described as "simple enough to use", but also "fiddly to use" and "slow to respond". Score: -0.10.
*   **smartphone_connect_rating**: Smartphone projection, Bluetooth connectivity, Apple CarPlay and Android Auto compatibility standard. Good for its era. Score: 0.10.
*   **audio_rating**: Six speakers standard. Score: 0.00.
*   **usb_ports**: USB connection standard. Likely 1 USB port. Score: -0.50.
*   **comfort_feature_score**: Recaro shell-backed sports front seats (standard), Leather flat-bottomed steering wheel, Sports pedals. Heated windscreen standard. Heated front seats optional (part of Winter Pack). Score: 0.30.
*   **convenience_feature_score**: Cruise control, Heated windscreen, Electrically adjustable/heated door mirrors. Lacks parking sensors/camera as standard (optional Technical Pack). Score: 0.00.
*   **brand_prestige_rating**: Vauxhall is a mainstream brand. VXR sub-brand adds performance prestige. Score: -0.30.
*   **model_prestige_rating**: Corsa is an entry-level model. VXR is the performance flagship. Score: -0.50.
*   **trim_prestige_rating**: VXR is the top performance trim. Score: -0.50.
*   **interior_luxury_rating**: Interior described as a marked improvement on previous generation, quality is up there with rivals, well-finished. However, aside from seats and steering wheel, it feels like a standard Corsa inside, basic materials elsewhere. Score: -0.30.
*   **interior_tech_focus_rating**: 7-inch touchscreen infotainment standard. Standard tech for a performance model of its era, not screen-forward. Score: -0.20.

